[111.569579, "o", "PASSAGE_0021: 7.3\tEstablished and Other Potentially Significant Drug Interactions\r\nTable 2 provides a listing of clinically significant drug interactions, including contraindicated drugs . Drugs listed in Table 2 ar\r\nPASSAGE_0022: ↑ alfuzosin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential hypotension .\r\nPASSAGE_0023: ↑ tamsulosin\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0024: ↑ ranolazine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions .\r\nPASSAGE_0025: ↑ antiarrhythmic\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for cardiac arrhythmias .\r\nPASSAGE_0027: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\nPASSAGE_0029: ↑ anticancer drugs\r\nAvoid co-administration of encorafenib or ivosidenib due to potential risk of serious adverse events such as QT interval prolongation. Avoid use of neratinib, venetoclax or ibrutini\r\nPASSAGE_0031: ↑ rivaroxaban\r\nIncreased bleeding risk with rivaroxaban. Avoid concomitant use.\r\ndabigatranSee Pharmacokinetics, Clinical Drug Interaction Studies (12.3).\r\n"]
[111.569659, "o", "PASSAGE_0032: ↑ dabigatran\r\nIncreased bleeding risk with dabigatran. Depending on dabigatran indication and renal function, reduce dose of dabigatran or avoid concomitant use. Refer to the dabigatran product label f\r\nPASSAGE_0034: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\nPASSAGE_0038: ↓ voriconazole\r\nAvoid concomitant use of voriconazole.\r\nPASSAGE_0041: ↑ colchicine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious and/or life-threatening reactions in patients with renal and/or hepatic impairment .\r\nPASSAGE_0045: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance. Alternate antimycobacterial drugs such as rifabutin should be considered"]
[111.569764, "o", "\r\nPASSAGE_0048: ↑ lurasidone↑ pimozide\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to serious and/or life-threatening reactions such as cardiac arrhythmias .\r\nPASSAGE_0051: ↑ silodosin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for postural hypotension .\r\nPASSAGE_0054: ↑ eplerenone\r\nCo-administration with eplerenone is contraindicated due to potential for hyperkalemia .\r\nPASSAGE_0055: ↑ ivabradine\r\nCo-administration with ivabradine is contraindicated due to potential for bradycardia or conduction disturbances .\r\nPASSAGE_0056: aliskiren,ticagrelor,vorapaxar\r\n                                       clopidogrel\r\n↑ aliskiren↑ ticagrelor↑ vorapaxar\r\n↓ clopidogrel active metabolite\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0059: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\nPASSAGE_0063: ↑ dihydroergotamine↑ ergotamine↑ methylergonovine\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute ergot toxicity characterized by vasospasm and ischemia of the extremities and other tissu\r\nPASSAGE_0065: glecaprevir/pibrentasvir\r\nAvoid concomitant use of glecaprevir/pibrentasvir with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0068: ↓ nirmatrelvir/ritonavir\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential loss of virologic response and possible resistance .\r\nPASSAGE_0069: ↑ lovastatin↑ simvastatin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for myopathy including rhabdomyolysis .\r\nIf treatment with PAXLOVID is considered medically necessary, discontinue use of lo"]
[111.569792, "o", "\r\nPASSAGE_0072: ↑ voclosporin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for acute and/or chronic nephrotoxicity .\r\nPASSAGE_0074: ↑ cyclosporine↑ tacrolimus\r\nAvoid concomitant use of calcineurin inhibitors with PAXLOVID when close monitoring of immunosuppressant concentrations is not feasible. If co-administered, dose adjustment \r\nPASSAGE_0075: ↑ everolimus↑ sirolimus\r\nAvoid concomitant use of everolimus and sirolimus and PAXLOVID.\r\nRefer to the individual immunosuppressant product label and latest guidelines for further information.\r\nPASSAGE_0078: ↑ salmeterol\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID. The combination may result in increased risk of cardiovascular adverse events associated with salmeterol, including QT prolongation, palpitations, and\r\nPASSAGE_0079: ↑ lomitapide\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for hepatotoxicity and gastrointestinal adverse reactions .\r\nPASSAGE_0080: ↑ eletriptan\r\nCo-administration of eletriptan within at least 72 hours of PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions including cardiovascular and cerebrovascular events \r\nPASSAGE_0081: ↑ ubrogepant\r\nCo-administration of ubrogepant with PAXLOVID is contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions .\r\nPASSAGE_0082: ↑ rimegepant\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0083: ↑ finerenone\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for serious adverse reactions including hyperkalemia, hypotension, and hyponatremia .\r\n"]
[111.56988, "o", "PASSAGE_0087: ↑ suvorexant\r\nAvoid concomitant use of suvorexant with PAXLOVID.\r\nPASSAGE_0089: ↑ naloxegol\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to the potential for opioid withdrawal symptoms .\r\nPASSAGE_0090: ↑ sildenafil\r\nCo-administration of sildenafil with PAXLOVID is contraindicated for use in pulmonary hypertension due to the potential for sildenafil associated adverse events, including visual abnormal\r\nPASSAGE_0091: ↑ tadalafil\r\nAvoid concomitant use of tadalafil with PAXLOVID for pulmonary hypertension.\r\nPASSAGE_0095: ↑ triazolam↑ midazolam\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for extreme sedation and respiratory depression .\r\nPASSAGE_0098: ↑ flibanserin\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for hypotension, syncope, and CNS depression .\r\nPASSAGE_0099: ↑ tolvaptan\r\nCo-administration contraindicated due to potential for dehydration, hypovolemia and hyperkalemia .\r\n"]
