[210.08292, "o", "    \"answer\": \"Medications that should be avoided or are contraindicated with Paxlovid include strong CYP3A inhibitors/substrates such as alfuzosin, tamsulosin, ranolazine, amiodarone, dronedarone, flecainide, propafenone, quinidine, lurasidone, pimozide, silodosin, eplerenone, ivabradine, dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, methylergonovine, lovastatin, simvastatin, voclosporin, lomitapide, eletriptan, ubrogepant, finerenone, naloxegol, sildenafil (for pulmonary arterial hypertension), triazolam, oral midazolam, flibanserin, and tolvaptan. Additionally, strong CYP3A inducers such as apalutamide, carbamazepine, phenobarbital, phenytoin, rifampin, and St. John\\'s wort must be avoided as they decrease Paxlovid exposure.\",\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
